# The images the package builders and their checks run in, by digest. Read by
# build-rpm.sh, build-pacman.sh and tests/packaging/*. A tag is a moving name,
# so a rebuild of the same release could land in another environment with
# nothing in history saying which; the digest cannot move.
#
# Measured 2026-11-23:
#   AlmaLinux 9    rpm 4.16.1.3: writes package format 4 and is the oldest rpm
#                  the channel serves (EL 9). The index digest, so the same
#                  line works on an x86_64 and an arm64 runner.
#   Fedora rawhide rpm 6.1: reads the RPMFORMAT tag the channel's check prints
#                  (rpm 4.16 does not know that tag).
#   Arch Linux     bsdtar and zstd are in the base image, which is all the
#                  pacman builder runs; pacman 7.1.
RPM_BUILD_BASE="docker.io/library/almalinux@sha256:02df05719ef287ebd0df0a1eedb9172a00bd70703aed7b25660e426b8e0d6047"
RPM_QUERY_IMAGE="registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora@sha256:4370ff149ccf5712fc5d2cb1a964825412350d775de6b629ddb0b4b2b864d76c"
PACMAN_BUILD_BASE="docker.io/library/archlinux@sha256:fcee73ea1b96e236248f53a213f71276cc9072d9025b58bce9915e32f19963ae"
